 "summary": "The file states the existence of a connected bipartite 2-degenerate graph H on Fin q such that ex(n,H) ≥ c·n^{3/2+ε} for all large n. It adds that no proper 2-colouring has a side of maximum degree ≤ 2. It also states that Erdős's r-degenerate conjecture, ex(n,H)=O(n^{2−1/r}) for bipartite r-degenerate H, is false. The statements look faithful; the main caveat is that the first theorem carries an extra conjunct beyond the paper's Theorem 1.2, which makes it stronger.",
